[previewyoutube="Te2z81yzwSE;full"][/previewyoutube][p]Congratulations to everyone on the first birthday of the Corsairs Legacy game!

[b]One year ago[/b], [b]we opened[/b] [b]Early Access[/b] to the Corsairs Legacy game, where we showed its basic mechanics.

We understood the risk of an unsuccessful start because the game level was far from what we had planned. However, we are an indie studio, and the lack of external funding pushed us to make precisely this decision: [b]to open access to the game and continue working on it, taking into account the feedback and suggestions of the players[/b].

Initial sales were lower than we expected, forcing us to make significant changes in the organization of the development process and the vision of the final result. We had to cut all possible costs and significantly reduce the number of team members.

From the beginning, we wanted to create a [b]high-quality game[/b] that players would enjoy, and we have not abandoned this goal.

We analyzed the feedback from the players and saw that in the first three years of full development, [b]we made the necessary foundation for the game[/b]. Now, there was an opportunity and a need to implement an open world and fill it with content.

The first major update after the start of early access had to wait five months, during which time we were moving the game from story rails to an open world. Then, we tried to release one major monthly update and minor updates with edits occasionally.

Today, we are releasing [b]the seventh big content update and launching a holiday game sale on [url="https://store.steampowered.com/app/1594880/"]Steam[/url][/b]. This year, we have increased the percentage of positive reviews from 37% at the start to 70+ % and increased the average playing time of players in the game from 2 to 11 hours. When the game is fully released, we plan to have 20-30 hours of interesting content in the open world and continue to develop it afterward.

Today's update adds [b]new game mechanics and additional content to the open world[/b]:
[/p][olist][*][p][b]We added treasure mechanics[/b]. After defeating an enemy ship captain, the player can find a map of the deceased captain with information on where he kept all his fortune. The map description will help the player understand which island to look for the dead captain's chest. Once you are at the desired location, you can activate the marker, which will lead you to the treasure;

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/9e6298d678106bc5ffbb84c3ee9535578d43bad8.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p][b]Battles of enemy squadrons have been added[/b] to the global map, which the player can join;

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/f1f8b7f898a202521fbf4e16cffa6251703f7857.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p]You can now [b]access all the achievements available on Steam[/b]. We have removed all the outdated ones and added relevant ones;

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/a299f59c87a17f7937fb1a50b607a12d27710879.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p][b]We added the mechanics of wear and tear of[/b] cold [b]weapons[/b] and firearms from their usage and added items for their care. If the player does not monitor the weapon's condition, it reduces its quality level and characteristics after reaching a critical state. You can increase the quality level of weapons at blacksmiths using the necessary items;

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/19277ab075f2f5ab6704369cb61f4c8ed9ea0197.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p]We added [b]background conversations of characters[/b] that can be heard while passing by;

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/7ccc1140af312b0b7a13869e9bedb0e2be43302f.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p][b]We added the death of the team[/b] due to hunger or disease in the event of a lack of food or medicine while sailing on the global map;[/p][/*][*][p]We added [b]a display of the player's ship in bays[/b] when the player is on islands;

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/84e09a03ed6e1bc9bd9846bf493e6bd6904c763f.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p][b]We[/b] significantly [b]redesigned[/b] [b]the key ground routes[/b] of the player's movement [b]around Bridgetown[/b]. Now, there is a new convenient passage between the store and the warehouse, as well as an improved route from the pier to the city;

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/87380804d8d6d1e121dec57799c12093076b9be2.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p][b]The visual part of Bridgetown has been improved[/b];

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/82b8ded85f9020b280e6725be27e9efb825b5921.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p]We were able to [b]return[/b] [b]the day change system[/b] to the global map without degrading the new, improved visual of the global map;

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/397d9eb9853d79cc7ba8c6a279b79cfbfb928d39.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p][b]Additional blacksmiths[/b] have [b]appeared[/b] in all towns;

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/73b4577dfd11056d52851f4a09762acc8fd78f1e.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p]We added [b]a new system for sorting items[/b] in the backpack and at street traders;

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/c1d70e82682747366799d5f9ac1dcc19571e9d4b.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p][b]Sleeping in the[/b] [b]tavern[/b] now also [b]restores energy[/b];[/p][/*][*][p][b]Night and rain lighting[/b] options have been [b]added to the Bridgetown tavern[/b];

[img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/cf34b1ac150699ee1bb4810bce64e4387a413a29.png"][/img]
[/p][/*][*][p][b]Rain sound has been added[/b] to the [b]prison[/b] and [b]Bridgetown[/b] [b]tavern[/b] locations;[/p][/*][*][p][b]We added many new sounds[/b]: opening a chest, taking items out of a backpack, sounds for the actions “chose” and “hide” weapons;[/p][/*][*][p]We fixed the problem of constant rain;[/p][/*][*][p]We fixed the problem of two background soundtracks in the cemetery;[/p][/*][*][p]We fixed the problem of the game freezing when opening the trade window;[/p][/*][*][p]We fixed the NPCs in the Tobago tavern;[/p][/*][*][p]We [b]fixed the amount of money[/b] that the player will receive [b]for transporting a passenger[/b] if he manages to increase the cost of the trip using charisma;[/p][/*][*][p][b]We fixed numerous bugs [/b]you wrote to us about and that we saw in analytics. We reworked the walls in boarding scenes, so if you still have NPCs or the main character falling overboard, or the boarding does not end (even though all enemies are killed), write to us about it.[/p][/*][/olist][p][img src="{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/b9eb7bbddba720be77cb100e73140b6dbb8e4d46.png"][/img] Since the last video diary, released 2 months ago, we have released three significant and two minor updates. We would like to note that the Tech-5 team traditionally helped us in working on all of them - they have been supporting Corsairs Legacy in technical matters since the first days of early access. Let's briefly talk about the [b]significant changes added[/b] to them:
[/p][olist][*][p][b]We added a system of new passenger delivery quests[/b] with different developments and achievements for them. Passengers can contact the main character in all five taverns, or you can start the quest yourself by talking to the tavern owner;[/p][/*][*][p]We implemented [b]the ability to buy and sell ships[/b] at the shipyard;[/p][/*][*][p]We added [b]a system of ship upgrades[/b] with the ability to apply 15 upgrades to any ship;[/p][/*][*][p][b]We added the ability to throw the cargo overboard and pick it up[/b] from sunken ships, receiving additional experience for this;[/p][/*][*][p]The game now has [b]21 ship skills available[/b] to the player after reaching level 10;[/p][/*][*][p]At the audience's request on Steam, [b]we added tips for the player to the loading screen[/b]. We have divided all the game features into categories according to game mechanics, and the player will see advice on precisely the mechanics that will be available after loading;[/p][/*][*][p][b]The combat system has been significantly reworked[/b]: delays from pressing a key to the hero's action in battle have been reduced; additional animation interruptions have been added for more dynamic gameplay;[/p][/*][*][p][b]The combat dynamics have been increased[/b], and the enemy AI logic has been improved;[/p][/*][*][p]A [b]new intro video[/b] has been added at the beginning of the game.[/p][/*][/olist][p]See you in the vastness of Corsairs Legacy![/p]

[b]Functional changes:[/b]
[olist]
[*] A bug with disappearing gift gun, saber, and clothes for Supporter Pack owners was fixed;
[*] Disappiaring of the protagonist's spawn point when pressing "continue" after the update was fixed;
[*] Some sounds and background dimming were added to the trade window;
[*] The cost of a regular yatagan was fixed;
[*] Loot and game balance were changed;
[*] The loot drop logic was changed: more valuable items dropped from captains, cheaper items dropped from sailors and soldiers;
[*] New food items were added: cocoa and corn.
[/olist]

[b]NPC edits:[/b]
[olist]
[*] Animations of the tavern owner in Bridgetown were added;
[*] Changes were made to the logic of the NPCs appearance in the frame (some problems still remain);
[*] Turning of Claire's head towards the player when talking to her in the arena was added;
[*] The radius of interaction with merchants has been increased so that you can start a conversation from any point around the merchant;
[*] After entering the arena location, NPCs in the arena immediately fight instead of running to each other;
[*] The situation when one sailor during boarding does not take part in the battle was fixed;
[*] Changes have been made to the calculation of NPC physics, resulting in higher FPS.
[/olist]

[b]Visual edits:[/b]
[olist]
[*] The water removed from the boats;
[*] All pads were fixed;
[*] Invisible walls removed according to messages in the Discord community;
[*] Changes have been made to the rocks;
[*] Reflection of light from surfaces in the city was fixed;
[*] Some secret paths for future quests were added.
[/olist]

We continue to expand the game, and, step by step, we are getting closer to adding free play to Corsairs Legacy.

Below you can see the list of changes included in the update:
[olist]
[*] now you can sell and buy things from merchants and apothecaries;
[*] role model added: experience, hero levels, characteristics, skills, and abilities;
[*] the city of Bridgetown with the possibility of free movement added;
[*] Bridgetown Tavern added (now you can visit it);
[*] it is now possible to play Perudo in Bridgetown Tavern;
[*] an arena became available with the opportunity to fight on it and thus earn additional funds, pump up the hero;
[*] mission to free Argyle from prison expanded (now it is necessary to complete the mission of the shift chief in the city);
[*] loot system rebalanced;
[*] when moving on land, accelerated mode has x3 time acceleration instead of x2;
[*] the ability to skip the victory animation during boarding was added;
[*] AI bug when playing perudo and AI has one die left was fixed;
[*] after the capture of pinas in the waters of Barbados, the video now works correctly (previously, only the audio in the second part of the video was played);
[*] names to workers with boxes in the smugglers' settlement were added;
[*] fixed French and German subtitles in Chapter 6;
[*] optimized physics of NPCs for the possibility of increasing the number of NPCs in the city (in case of fixing strange behavior of NPCs, send a video to Discord or mail);
[*] changes were made to the quest descriptions based on players’ feedback from the feedback form and Discord.
[/olist]

The plan for the next update is to add the ability to start the game in Bridgetown without going through the story's first chapters. A separate parameter of the "new game" will be the ability to disable hints.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/4d059bcb5bba64638d16f9d64edeac61ab26cd48.jpg[/img]

We appreciate all of your feedback on Corsairs Legacy. Our team analyzed it, and from the release day began to work on changes that players wanted to see. [b]The first Early Access update for Corsairs Legacy was released today[/b], and we will continue to [b]expand the game regularly[/b].

Below you can find [b]the list of changes[/b] included [b]in the update[/b]:
[olist][*]
you can capture and transfer to any ship in the game;
[/*][*]
the gameplay logic of the quests changed; markers have been removed in some places so that players can solve the quests on their own;
[/*][*]
the required amount of land movement reduced;
[/*][*]
all chests in Barbados now have loot;
[/*][*]
during ground battles, a marker has been added to enemies above their heads, informing about an attack on the main character (similar to Assassin's Creed: Unity) to increase the ability to parry a blow;
[/*][*]
the operation of the camera on the stairs in the prison fixed;
[/*][*]
fixed a critical bug of the absence of Spanish soldiers on the Tobago beach;
[/*][*]
fixed bug with invisible English soldiers in prison and lighthouse.
[/*][/olist]
[b]Note! The new version removes the progress. Progress saving will be added in the next update.[/b]

List of [b]tasks[/b] that should be included [b]in the next few updates[/b]:
[olist][*]
traders will appear in the game;
[/*][*]
the possibility of character development will be added;
[/*][*]
the city of Bridgetown will be added;
[/*][*]
additional side activities will appear;
[/*][*]
an opportunity to usefully spend all earned funds will be added.
[/*][/olist]
We've decided to focus all efforts on expanding Corsairs Legacy and [b]put plans for future releases on hold[/b] [b]until[/b] the current [b]game is refined[/b] with player feedback.

For us to be able to improve and expand Corsairs Legacy, it is important to have stable sales, and for this, we need to have a [b]positive rating on Steam[/b]. If you agree with our direction of development, please leave a [url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/1594880/][b]positive review on Steam[/b][/url] so that the game can reach a higher user rating. We will be very grateful to you.

[previewyoutube=9g67vTbnujo;full][/previewyoutube]
Today we will be answering your questions, and in today’s devlog you’ll get to know:

[list]
[*] How many people are developing “Corsairs Legacy”? Who are those people?
[*] Why are we developing the game in Unity and not in Unreal Engine?
[*] Do we contact people that were developing “Sea Dogs” (with the original team Seaward)?
[*] Why can’t our team unite with BlackMark Studio to achieve shared results?
[/list]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/e9e0a6b0b2c6a25280974600862d4411cc822c58.jpg[/img]

Well, let’s start with [b]the team[/b]. The project is currently being developed by a company called [url=https://mauris.info/]Mauris[/url] that was founded in 2013 and its current director is Volodymyr Bondarenko. Since 2013, Mauris has developed over 80 projects for companies like Bosch, Freedom Finance, Nomad Insurance, Hettich, Compendium, Bionorica, Teva, Sandoz, BI Group.

After talking to the art director of “Sea Dogs 4”, Yuri Rogach, we decided to make a pilot version of an RPG in 3D and understand the complexity of development. We decided that it’s entirely possible and Mauris started to search for specialists in a PC game dev field that would be responsible for developing the future game. We spent 4 months on market research, analyzing pirate projects, defining a movement vector, and forming a team. With the growth of the project, we started expanding our team, and here’s who works on the game today:

[list]
[*] three Unity programmers;
[*] level designer;
[*] lighting specialist;
[*] environment modeler;
[*] character modeler;
[*] editor;
[*] voiceover specialist;
[*] video editing specialist;
[*] designer;
[*] illustrator;
[*] two animators;
[*] back-end programmer;
[*] special effects specialist;
[*] translator.
[/list]
Our team liaises with developers of the original “Sea Dogs”, but[b] None of the Seaward members are contributing to the development of Corsairs Legacy[/b] at the moment. 

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/b6282a91dd6947dbbfb0bd23e5e9aad3ae4bbc6b.jpg[/img]

Now, let’s talk about [b]Unity and Unreal Engine[/b]. Mauris always emphasized high-quality development and the first 4 employees, including the director, are programmers. Having a lot of experience in development, we understand that it’s better to work with technologies that the team has competence in. Using those technologies makes it possible to make the best possible product. At the time of creating a project’s strategy, we were talking to the leading programmer of the “City of Abandoned Ships”, Eduard Zaitsev, who had long experience of developing in Unity. He thinks that to create a game similar to “Sea Dogs” it doesn’t matter whether to choose Unity or Unreal Engine. A good result can be achieved in both engines.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40369036/fdcf7c87d50feb8f1919ea63247c73a817de5f70.jpg[/img]

And lastly, we’ll answer [b]why we can’t unite with BlackMark Studio[/b] to achieve the result. There are many reasons. The first one is – BlackMark team consists of modders, who develop a game on Storm Engine in their free time. Our team consists of Unity programmers who develop Corsairs Legacy full-time. As a result, we have different work inputs and specializations.

The second reason is that we make different games for different audiences. BlackMark Studio initially focuses on the audience of “Sea Dogs”, on people who know the game well and would like to see an interesting and complicated sequel. Our goal, on the other hand, is to attract many new audiences to Corsairs Legacy that would give a new life to the setting.

To find out all the details about the dev team of the game - watch the full devlog video :) Subscribe to our YouTube channels in order not to miss news about the Corsairs Legacy development!

